<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">warm like you</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;â€œAre you gonna help me with this or not?â€ Adora asks, rising onto her tiptoes so she can actually reach the top of the sodding tree that Catra had warned was gonna be too tall to decorate without a step ladder. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œNot.â€ Catra replies from where sheâ€™s sprawled inelegantly over the couch. Her tail swaying languidly over the cushions. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora huffs lightly. Before, and itâ€™s with an uncharacteristic level of caution, slipping the white and gold bauble in place on a branch above her head. â€œThatâ€™s not very helpful.â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œI never claimed to be,â€ Catra disputes, folding her arms. â€œBesides, youâ€™re the one who wanted the tree, I didnâ€™t sign up for any of this grunt work.â€ &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora, ironically, grunts like sheâ€™s finally accepting the refusal. Which is a shame really, because Catra doesnâ€™t think it would have taken much more for her to have rolled her eyes and joined her.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
